# This file exists so npm does NOT fall back to the repo's .gitignore when
# packing this package.
#
# The root .gitignore excludes commands/ensemble:*.md, because ':' is illegal
# on NTFS and committing those files makes the repo impossible to check out on
# Windows. They are still required in the published tarball — OMP derives its
# slash-command name from the filename, so the canonical "ensemble:<cmd>" form
# is what registers /ensemble:<cmd>. prepublishOnly regenerates them just
# before packing.
#
# Without this file, npm would apply .gitignore's rule and silently ship a
# tarball missing every colon-namespaced command.
#
# The "files" array in package.json is the real allowlist; nothing extra needs
# excluding here.
